Cell[TextData[{
 "Several oxidoreducases oxidize alcohol to aldehyde, and confer the reducing \
equivalents to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["NAD", "+"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e4e0f6c-ffe3-49f9-9db1-9dc3b89e6844"],
 ". Upon binding the alcohol, the enzyme is able to accept ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["NAD", "+"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f780393-2695-4400-aafd-a67d72f5e798"],
 ", and release the products quickly without detectable trinary intermediate \
EAB. \nHowever, an alternative may be the random sequential binding of either \
substrate. This random sequential reaction scheme may be analyzed by: "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965958735219982*^9, 3.965958742989127*^9}, {
  3.965958804342791*^9, 3.96595898653533*^9}, {3.965959016808948*^9, 
